@* The bento the landing page already had, now built from two components instead of a hand-written
   grid. Six cards fill a 3×3 exactly: one 2×2 and five single cells. The only layout left on a
   card is how far it spans, and that is one class — no "wide" or "large" variant to keep in step
   with the grid's column count. *@
<BentoGrid Class="w-full">
    <BentoCard Class="lg:col-span-2 lg:row-span-2">
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Native first</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>
                Dialogs, popovers, the select panel — all real platform primitives, so focus traps,
                escape-to-close, and the keyboard come from the browser rather than from a compiler.
            </CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="flex h-full items-end">
            <code class="rounded bg-muted px-2 py-1 text-xs">&lt;dialog&gt; · [popover] · &lt;select&gt;</code>
        </CardContent>
    </BentoCard>

    <BentoCard>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Token themes</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>Seventy themes, runtime switchable.</CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>
    </BentoCard>

    <BentoCard>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Accessible</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>ARIA reproduced from shadcn's own markup.</CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>
    </BentoCard>

    <BentoCard>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Fast</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>One CSS file, one JS file. Nothing else ships.</CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>
    </BentoCard>

    <BentoCard>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Server-first</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>No hydration, no client state to lose.</CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>
    </BentoCard>

    <BentoCard>
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Typed API</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>Parameters and slots, not a bag of strings.</CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>
    </BentoCard>
</BentoGrid>
